System Response: CHECK constraint added (validates instantly, 0 violations); ETL contract restored; rejections stop
Resolution: Root cause was a varchar->text migration that silently dropped a 20-char length invariant a downstream ETL depended on; re-imposing it as an explicit CHECK constraint rather than reverting the type restored the contract without risking truncation of live data.

Reasoning: External resolution works but every *.svc.cluster.local name NXDOMAINs right after a cluster-dns ConfigMap change -- that points at the CoreDNS Corefile's kubernetes zone, not the upstream path. First confirm the failure shape from inside a pod.
<|call:dns_lookup|> {"name": "payments.prod.svc.cluster.local", "from_pod": "shell/prod", "type": "A"}
System Response: ;; ->>HEADER<<- status: NXDOMAIN ; payments.prod.svc.cluster.local. ; AUTHORITY: cluster.local SOA (CoreDNS authoritative)
